    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Amwell is pivoting from low-acuity telehealth volume to higher-value care. Total platform visits are falling as subscription revenue churns, but Amwell Medical Group visit revenue is growing, driven by a shift to higher-acuity visits and surging virtual primary care adoption. This mix shift is improving unit economics, while the broader telehealth market’s maturation increasingly rewards integrated, higher-acuity solutions over commoditized low-acuity encounters.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Following a major transformation in 2025, leadership has sharply cut the cash burn and guided to operational cash-flow breakeven by the fourth quarter of 2026. The company maintains a strong net-cash position, providing ample runway. Consistent execution — including an earnings beat and upward revisions in analyst estimates — prompted a stock upgrade and is building credibility around management’s cost discipline and profitability timeline, though some debate over timing persists.",
